# Git branching

Create feature branches from `origin/nonprod`, never from `main` or another feature branch.

When starting implementation, if the current branch is `main` or `nonprod`:

1. Fetch `origin`.
2. Create and check out `feat/...` or `fix/...` from `origin/nonprod`.
3. Push the branch so CI runs.
4. Open a draft PR against `nonprod` if one does not exist: `gh pr create --base nonprod --draft`.

Never approve, merge, or enable auto-merge. Wait for CI (tests) to pass; the human reviews and approves afterwards.

PRs into `main` must come from `nonprod`.
